-- V9: curated, validated problem catalog.
--
-- Why: V6 contained 510 entries that were only 30 distinct problems (each repeated 17 times with a different
-- 'workshop' prefix), with one example, a placeholder constraint text, three tests of which one was a sample, no starter
-- code and no reference solutions. This migration:
--   1. archives the 480 duplicate copies (kept, not deleted, so any submission that points at them survives);
--   2. rewrites the 30 distinct legacy problems in place (same slug) with full statements, >= 2 examples,
--      real constraints, >= 2 sample tests and independent hidden tests;
--   3. adds new original problems across the core algorithm topics;
--   4. adds starter code for every language and verified reference solutions (Python, C++).
-- Every expected output below was produced by executing the reference solutions (see catalog/REPORT.md).
-- Re-running is safe: problems are upserted by slug and their tests/tags/starter code are replaced.

-- Tags (the legacy 'Bits' tag is renamed so the filter list has one bit-manipulation topic).
